                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A 2D physics puzzle game where the main concept is shooting portals that allow teleporting (the influence is obvious but this goes to its own direction).\n\nThere is possibly a potentially interesting game hidden somewhere here, but at the moment the execution makes this mostly frustrating: such a basic concept as deciding which type of portal you are shooting is missing, you always alternate between the two, and since they nevertheless require some positioning, the game becomes very annoying very quickly. And the swimming-in-jelly-physics do not exactly help. \n\nOnly one level is unlocked at a time so if you get stuck, no dice. And early on I already got to a level where I pretty much figured what I am supposed to do but with this execution trying to get this done would just take grinding to hit exactly the right pixels at exactly the right moments to get further, and frankly I'm not convinced it's worth the effort.",
